    release: cut v0.1.6 — one published naming + platform set across README/Makefile/CI. Addresses BT-036.
    
    BT-036: the published v0.1.5 asset (vcs.revision f9b40415) predates the SG-126
    fingerprint gate, and the three release surfaces disagreed about what a release
    even contains. This commit reconciles them to ONE naming + platform set and
    moves the pins to the tag being cut.
    
    Naming/platform agreement (deliverable A):
    - .github/workflows/multiarch.yml passes an explicit `platforms:` input. The org
      reusable workflow's default list drops linux/arm and freebsd/amd64 (and adds
      windows/arm64), so a tag-push cut published a different platform set than
      `make release`. The list now matches the Makefile's PLATFORMS in the same
      order, so both cut paths are interchangeable name-for-name.
    - Makefile `release` emits the CI names — boardctl_<goos>_<goarch>[.exe] plus
      dist/SHA256SUMS — instead of hyphen names + sha256sums.txt. The BT-030
      VERSION/tag guard is untouched. Two defects surfaced by actually running it:
      (1) `$(BINARY)_$os_$arch` is parsed by the shell as the variable `os_`, so the
      arch was silently DROPPED and 7 platforms collapsed onto 4 files; the shell
      variables are brace-quoted now (`$${os}_$${arch}`). (2) `make release` never
      cleared dist/, so a leftover hyphen-named binary would have been published as
      an extra asset alongside the new names; the recipe removes dist/ first.
    - README's install block downloads the names that actually exist (underscore
      assets + SHA256SUMS), the platform claim names the published set (linux
      amd64/arm64/arm, darwin amd64/arm64, windows amd64, freebsd amd64), and
      "Cutting a release" now documents the CI tag-push as the primary cut path with
      `make release` as the offline/local equivalent (same names, `gh release
      create ... dist/*` line included). The retired "make release is the only
      sanctioned path" claim is replaced.
    
    The CI cut could not have fired at all before this commit: the workflow's push
    trigger was branches-only, and GitHub skips tag refs when only `branches:` is
    defined, while the reusable workflow's Release job runs on tag refs only. Added
    `tags: ["v*"]`.
    
    dedupe-board (deliverable B): documented honestly as source-only — every
    published asset is the boardctl CLI — with its acquisition path
    (`go install github.com/coding-hermes/boardctl/cmd/dedupe-board@latest`) next to
    the usage lines and marked source-only in the repository-layout table. No claim
    that it ships in a release asset.
    
    Pins (deliverable D): every README release surface moves to v0.1.6 — the
    `Current release:` line, both install URLs, the version/--json examples and the
    release procedure — so `make version-check` passes.
    
    Regression guard: internal/versioncheck's TestVersioncheck is already the
    in-process release-surface gate shared by three enforcement surfaces (`make
    version-check`, the CI "Version-check" step with the byte-identical command, and
    plain `go test ./...`), so the new assertions went there rather than into a new
    package or a fourth gate: README must download the underscore asset + SHA256SUMS
    for the pinned tag and must not name the retired spellings; the Makefile must
    build `_${os}_${arch}` names and write SHA256SUMS; the workflow's platform list
    must equal the Makefile's PLATFORMS in order; the workflow must keep a `tags:`
    trigger. RED-proved by mutating each surface in turn (hyphen names,
    sha256sums.txt, a one-entry platform drift, a removed tags: trigger): each one
    FAILS the gate naming the surface, the unmutated control is green, and both
    files were restored byte-identically (sha256 verified).
    
    Verified before commit: go build ./..., go vet ./..., go test -count=1 -short
    ./... all ok; make fmt-check, make version-check, make vuln-check green;
    gofmt -l cmd internal prints nothing; `make release` emits the 7 underscore
    binaries + dist/SHA256SUMS and dist/boardctl_linux_amd64 prints "boardctl
    version v0.1.5" (the pre-cut tag, correct — v0.1.6 is created by this commit's
    tag).
    
    Cut path: `git tag v0.1.6` on this commit, then push the branch and the tag; the
    Release job cross-builds the 7 platforms, writes SHA256SUMS, attests provenance
    and publishes the release. The published-asset proof (sha256sum -c, `version`
    -> v0.1.6, go version -m vcs.revision == the tag commit) is recorded in the
    foreman tick record.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
